+### Permission modes
+
+Set the server's `HYPR_AGENT_PORTAL_PERMISSION_MODE` environment variable before
+starting its MCP process. Restart the server after changing it.
+
+| Mode | Application permission default | Confirmation default |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `standard` (default) | View-only unless explicitly authorized | External confirmation for high-risk actions |
+| `read-only` | Observation only; mutation tools hidden | Mutations disabled |
+| `full` (alias `unrestricted`) | Full application and clipboard access | No confirmation prompts |
+
+`full` permits launches, input, saves and high-risk actions without a token.
+It also disables server-level global input-grab, layer and takeover gates.
+It supplies defaults; explicitly configured app permissions, confinement,
+clipboard restrictions and read-only settings still apply. Panic, session-lock
+handling, target identity validation and input serialization are runtime controls
+and remain active. This is a server authorization setting, not a native plugin
+ABI or sandbox change.
+
+For partial access without prompts, keep `standard`, authorize the desired apps,
+and set `HYPR_AGENT_PORTAL_APPROVAL_POLICY=never`. The other value, `external`,
+retains physical confirmation. Canonical `SECURITY_PERMISSION_MODE` and
+`SECURITY_APPROVAL_POLICY` names take precedence over short aliases. Invalid
+values reject startup. `security_status` reports the effective permission mode
+and confirmation policy. Tool arguments cannot change these settings.
+
+Example Codex configuration:
+
+```toml
+[mcp_servers.hypr_agent_portal]
+command = "python3"
+args = ["/absolute/path/to/mcp/hypr-agent-portal-mcp.py"]
+default_tools_approval_mode = "approve"
+
+[mcp_servers.hypr_agent_portal.env]
+HYPR_AGENT_PORTAL_PERMISSION_MODE = "full"
+```
+
+Codex's `default_tools_approval_mode` controls the client's prompts. Portal's
+permission mode controls the server's authorization. They are independent.
+
